existing body rule).\n\nIn `@src/components/domain/CardNumbersField.tsx`:\n- Around line 39-52: handleBlur currently only sets error states on failure\npaths and never clears previous errors on success; update the handleBlur\nfunction (referencing handleBlur, setErrorStatus, and\nCARD_NUMBER_LENGTH_PER_INPUT) so that after the empty and length checks pass you\nexplicitly call setErrorStatus(null) (e.g., at the end of the function or in the\nsuccessful branch) to clear any prior error state.\n\nIn `@src/components/domain/CVCField.tsx`:\n- Around line 40-52: handleBlur only sets errorStatus for failure cases and\nnever clears it on success, so previous error states (like 'numberOnly') can\npersist; update the handleBlur function (which uses CVC_LENGTH and calls\nsetErrorStatus) to explicitly clear/reset the error state in the success path\nafter all validations pass (e.g., call setErrorStatus to a neutral value such as\nnull or 'none') so valid CVC inputs remove any prior error indications.\n\nIn `@src/components/domain/ExpirationPeriodField.tsx`:\n- Around line 60-73: handleBlur currently sets 'required' or 'invalidLength' but\nleaves prior errors (numberOnly/invalidMonth/invalidYear) intact when those\nchecks pass; after the two early returns in handleBlur (the checks against ''\nand PERIOD_LENGTH_PER_INPUT) add a success branch that clears the error state by\ncalling setErrorStatus to the \"no error\" value your component uses (e.g., null\nor empty string), ensuring handleBlur resets any previous error codes when input\npasses validation; keep setCurrentIndex(index) as-is.\n\nIn `@src/components/ui/Card.tsx`:\n- Around line 15-16: Update the hardcoded image src to use the Vite base URL so\nsubpath deployments work: replace src=\"/visa.png\" and src=\"/mastercard.png\" with\nsrc={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}visa.png`} and\nsrc={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}mastercard.png`} in the Card component (the JSX\nthat uses cardBrand and cardBrandStyle). Also add a unique key prop to the list\nrendering in this component (where the cards/items are mapped and rendered on\nlines ~21-22)—ensure each mapped element uses a stable identifier (e.g., item.id\nor index if no id) as key.\n\nIn `@src/pages/AddCardPage.tsx`:\n- Around line 64-68: The form in AddCardPage.tsx lacks an onSubmit handler so\npressing Enter will trigger a native submit and reload the page; add an onSubmit\nprop to the <form> (the element that wraps CardNumbersField,\nExpirationPeriodField, CVCField) that calls event.preventDefault() (and\noptionally delegates to your existing submit logic if any) to stop the browser's\ndefault submit/refresh behavior; implement the handler as a local function\n(e.g., handleFormSubmit) and pass it to the form's onSubmit attribute so\nhandleCardNumbersUpdate / handleExpirationPeriodUpdate / handleCVCUpdate flows\nare preserved and state isn't lost.\n\nIn `@src/reset.css`:\n- Around line 85-97: The CSS block for the legend selector contains unnecessary\nblank lines that trigger stylelint's declaration-empty-line-before rule; open\nthe legend rule (selector \"legend\") and remove the empty lines between\ndeclarations (between display, width/max-width, padding/margin, and\nfont/line-height/color) so each declaration sits directly on its own line\nwithout extra blank lines, then re-run lint to confirm the rule violations are\nresolved.\n\nIn `@src/utils.ts`:\n- Around line 3-8: categorizeCardBrand currently accesses cardNumbers[0] without\nchecking for an empty array which can throw; modify categorizeCardBrand to first\nguard that CardInfo['cardNumbers'] is non-empty (and that cardNumbers[0] is a\nstring) and if it's empty/invalid immediately return the default brand 'local',\notherwise proceed with the existing logic (the startsWith('4') check and the\nfirstTwoNumber parse/range checks).\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@src/components/ui/FormField.stories.tsx`:\n- Around line 29-33: The label element inside the FormField story is not\nassociated with the Input, hurting accessibility; update the story so the\n<label> has an htmlFor that matches an id on the Input (e.g., set id=\"cvc\" on\nthe Input and htmlFor=\"cvc\" on the label) and do the same for the other similar\nstory instance (the other FormField/Input pair). Ensure the id is stable/unique\nfor the story (use args.id if available) and keep Input's variant logic\nunchanged.\n\nIn `@src/components/ui/FormField.tsx`:\n- Around line 20-23: FormField currently renders error text but doesn't\nprogrammatically link it to the input; update the FormField component to\ngenerate a stable unique id (use React.useId or a ref) for the error caption,\ngive FieldCaption that id and role=\"alert\", and clone the children React element\n(when React.isValidElement(children)) to inject aria-describedby={error ?\nerrorId : undefined} and aria-invalid={!!error}; keep fallback spacing when no\nerror. Reference: FormField component, children prop, FieldCaption, error and\nerrorMessage.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪄 Autofix (Beta)</summary>\n\nFix all unresolved CodeRabbit comments on this PR:\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"4b0d0e0a-96d7-4f10-b296-3a18ea78f0b9\"} --> Push a commit to this branch (recommended)\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"ff5b1114-7d8c-49e6-8ac1-43f82af23a33\"} --> Create a new PR with the fixes\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: Organization UI\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n**Run ID**: `fe5d63a8-327c-4ae3-aadc-d832cbd2639c`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 8d4c2c73f7cce87ffaae55245ae1cfd10228981d and c46299ed171719ff1214609e851f21d2c678e0a3.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (5)</summary>\n\n* `package-lock.json` is excluded by `!**/package-lock.json`\n* `public/favicon.svg`